ot \\pi )=sec⁡(x+20\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $sec⁡x=2\\sqrt{5},$ then $sec⁡(x+20\\pi )=2\\sqrt{5}.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5}sec⁡(x+20\\pi )-3 & =\\sqrt{5}(2\\sqrt{5})-3 \\\\  & =2(5)-3 \\\\  & =10-3 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246936 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246937 13194139533688 true] [17592186246936 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246938 13194139533688 true] [17592186246936 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246939 13194139533688 true] [17592186246936 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246940 13194139533688 true] [17592186246936 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246941 13194139533688 true] [17592186246936 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533688 true] [17592186246936 1041 "selection" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246936 1104 #edb/ref 17592186246940 13194139533688 true] [17592186246936 1110 #uuid "b298d044-0e1c-5362-bce8-97960a068140" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246937 1034 "13" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246937 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533688 true] [17592186246937 1111 #uuid "672b8aab-6b54-5332-94d9-88022cf192e0" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246938 1034 "-7" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246938 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533688 true] [17592186246938 1111 #uuid "b8d2bbb4-01c2-5fbc-b253-6b7233f4add2" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246939 1034 "9" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246939 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533688 true] [17592186246939 1111 #uuid "3ec72097-381b-5e0e-9977-3b0c849d756a" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246940 1034 "7" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246940 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533688 true] [17592186246940 1111 #uuid "99a5203b-a8a8-5dfa-9780-e39174d23215" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246941 1034 "-13" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246941 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533688 true] [17592186246941 1111 #uuid "aa86e5a1-565e-502e-bfaa-c81ddba1596a" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246942 1017 #edb/ref 17592186246943 13194139533688 true] [17592186246942 1089 "q-136623" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246942 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533688 true] [17592186246942 1100 "If $sec⁡x=-2,$ then $5sec⁡(-x+12\\pi )+1=$" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246942 1113 #uuid "ae3cb1bd-2bc1-5766-9ec9-742fa9428ab0" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246942 1138 false 13194139533688 true] [17592186246942 1145 "First, let's recall the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934039/assets/fbf6ef1ca91f998ab4dc2dda1890ffc8a713f2eeff19e5569351b2466256d63a.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we note the following:\n\n- The period of $sec⁡x$ is $2\\pi .$\n\n- Our graph is symmetric about the $y$-axis. This means that $sec⁡x$ is an *even* function, and we have\n\n$$\nsec⁡(-x)=sec⁡x.\n$$\n\nLet's now evaluate our expression:\n\n- Firstly, using the periodicity of $sec⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sec⁡(-x+12\\pi ) & =sec⁡(-x+2\\pi \\cdot 6) \\\\  & =sec⁡(-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Secondly, using the evenness of $sec⁡x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sec⁡(-x) & =sec⁡x \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5sec⁡(-x+12\\pi )+1 & =5\\cdot (-2)+1 \\\\  & =-10+1 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246943 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246944 13194139533688 true] [17592186246943 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246945 13194139533688 true] [17592186246943 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246946 13194139533688 true] [17592186246943 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246947 13194139533688 true] [17592186246943 1000 #edb/ref 17592186246948 13194139533688 true] [17592186246943 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533688 true] [17592186246943 1041 "selection" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246943 1104 #edb/ref 17592186246945 13194139533688 true] [17592186246943 1110 #uuid "f9882397-8495-5e27-a125-069a29b3baf0" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246944 1034 "12" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246944 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533688 true] [17592186246944 1111 #uuid "750dfcdd-2a17-51e2-9e7f-6fb3bf9ce64d"