998 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533688 true] [17592186246998 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=sec⁡x?$\n\n- $x=-\\pi $ is not in the domain of the function. $$\n- $y=-\\frac{1}{3}$ is in the range of the function. $$\n- $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote." 13194139533688 true] [17592186246998 1113 #uuid "3d652f1a-c6ee-5796-966d-faf889bb3033" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246998 1138 false 13194139533688 true] [17592186246998 1145 "Let's plot the graph of $y=sec⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934039/assets/da729794a0331383debd75be0a4ce4a9f2d4da3286f50bd4f284868996077412.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is defined for all real numbers except the values $\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $ for any integer $n,$ thus it is defined for $x=-\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ),$ so $y=-\\frac{1}{3}$ is not in the range.\n\n- Statement III is true. The function $y=sec⁡x$ has vertical asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi $, thus $x=-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ is a vertical asymptote." 13194139533688 true] [17592186246999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247000 13194139533688 true] [17592186246999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247001 13194139533688 true] [17592186246999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247002 13194139533688 true] [17592186246999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247003 13194139533688 true] [17592186246999 1000 #edb/ref 17592186247004 13194139533688 true] [17592186246999 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533688 true] [17592186246999 1041 "selection" 13194139533688 true] [17592186246999 1104 #edb/ref 17592186247003 13194139533688 true] [17592186246999 1110 #uuid "ff1fe016-e077-5886-a3da-8039c1b98073" 13194139533688 true] [17592186247000 1034 "II and III only" 13194139533688 true] [17592186247000 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533688 true] [17592186247000 1111 #uuid "12e6da9f-695a-5581